 "font_size": 14,
 "html": "<!--\n\tSurvey Certificate \u2014 A4 landscape.\n\n\tEverything `doc.*` reads here is attached by `Survey Response.before_print`\n\t(see `survey.certification.build_certificate_context`), not by the fields\n\tthe DocType actually stores \u2014 a Survey Response has no `recipient_name` or\n\t`layout_family` field of its own.\n\n\tCompatibility note: colour and orientation come from literal hex values\n\tand the wkhtmltopdf `.print-format { orientation: ...; page-size: ...; }`\n\tconvention, never from CSS custom properties (`var(--x)`) or flexbox\n\t`margin: auto` centring \u2014 this print format is rendered by wkhtmltopdf's\n\tbundled Qt WebKit (~2015), which silently drops both. Every rule below\n\twas checked against that engine, not a modern browser.\n-->\n<style>\n.print-format {\n\torientation: Landscape;\n\tpage-size: A4;\n\tmargin-top: 0mm;\n\tmargin-bottom: 0mm;\n\tmargin-left: 0mm;\n\tmargin-right: 0mm;\n}\n\n* { box-sizing: border-box; }\n\nhtml, body {\n\tmargin: 0;\n\tpadding: 0;\n\tfont-family: \"Helvetica Neue\", Arial, sans-serif;\n\tcolor: #1f2933;\n\tbackground: #fdfcfb;\n}\n\nbody.family-classic { font-family: Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif; }\n\n.certificate { position: relative; width: 297mm; height: 210mm; }\n\n.frame {\n\tposition: absolute;\n\ttop: 8mm; left: 8mm;\n\twidth: 281mm; height: 194mm;\n\tborder: 0.6mm solid #6d28d9;\n}\n\n.frame-inner {\n\tposition: absolute;\n\ttop: 3mm; left: 3mm;\n\twidth: 275mm; height: 188mm;\n\tborder: 0.5mm solid #6d28d9;\n}\n\nbody.family-classic .frame-inner {\n\tborder-style: double; border-width: 1.1mm;\n\ttop: 2mm; left: 2mm; width: 277mm; height: 190mm;\n}\n\n.watermark {\n\tposition: absolute;\n\ttop: 130mm; left: 0mm; width: 297mm;\n\ttext-align: center;\n\tfont-size: 44pt;\n\tfont-weight: 700;\n\tletter-spacing: 0.3em;\n\tcolor: #f6d3cf;\n\ttext-transform: uppercase;\n}\n\n.not-passed-flag {\n\tposition: absolute;\n\ttop: 130mm; left: 0mm; width: 297mm;\n\ttext-align: center;\n\tfont-size: 16pt;\n\tfont-weight: 700;\n\tletter-spacing: 0.1em;\n\tcolor: #b42318;\n\ttext-transform: uppercase;\n}\n\n.main { position: relative; text-align: center; padding: 26mm 32mm 0; }\n\n.eyebrow {\n\tletter-spacing: 0.35em;\n\tfont-size: 10pt;\n\tcolor: #6d28d9;\n\ttext-transform: uppercase;\n\tmargin: 0 0 4mm;\n}\n\n.title { font-size: 28pt; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 6mm; }\nbody.family-classic .title { font-style: italic; font-weight: 400; }\n\n.lead { font-size: 11pt; color: #6b7280; margin: 0 0 3mm; }\n\n.recipient {\n\tdisplay: inline-block;\n\tmax-width: 220mm;\n\toverflow-wrap: break-word;\n\tfont-size: 24pt;\n\tfont-weight: 700;\n\tcolor: #6d28d9;\n\tmargin: 0 0 5mm;\n\tpadding: 0 4mm 3mm;\n\tborder-bottom: 0.4mm solid #ede9fe;\n\tmin-width: 130mm;\n}\n\n.survey-title {\n\tmax-width: 220mm;\n\toverflow-wrap: break-word;\n\tfont-size: 14pt;\n\tfont-weight: 600;\n\tmargin: 2mm auto 6mm;\n}\n\n.score-line { font-size: 11pt; color: #6b7280; margin: 0 0 1mm; }\n.score-line .value { color: #6d28d9; font-weight: 700; }\n.summary-line { font-size: 9pt; color: #6b7280; margin: 0; }\n\n.footer {\n\tposition: absolute;\n\tbottom: 20mm; left: 30mm; width: 237mm;\n\tdisplay: table;\n\ttable-layout: fixed;\n}\n\n.footer .cell { display: table-cell; vertical-align: bottom; }\n.footer .block { text-align: center; }\n.footer .seal-cell { text-align: center; }\n\n.footer .block .value {\n\tfont-size: 10pt; color: #1f2933;\n\tmargin: 0 0 1mm; font-weight: 600;\n}\n\n.footer .block .line {\n\tborder-top: 0.3mm solid #1f2933;\n\tpadding-top: 1.5mm; margin: 0;\n\tfont-size: 8.5pt; color: #6b7280;\n\tletter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase;\n}\n\n.seal { width: 24mm; height: 24mm; }\n\n/* The rings and star get their own colour directly rather than inheriting it\n   through `currentColor`: Frappe's own print stylesheet sets\n   `@media print { *, *:before, *:after { color: #000 } }`, and because `*`\n   matches these shapes directly, that beats inheritance from `.seal`\n   regardless of specificity \u2014 a direct match always wins over an inherited\n   value. Setting `fill`/`stroke` explicitly here sidesteps the question. */\n.seal-ring { stroke: #6d28d9; }\n.seal-star { fill: #6d28d9; }\n\n/* Modern adds the seal; classic stays unadorned and typographic. */\nbody.family-classic .seal-cell .seal { display: none; }\n\n/* Colour: purple is the unprefixed default (see build_certificate_context). */\nbody.colour-blue .eyebrow,\nbody.colour-blue .recipient,\nbody.colour-blue .score-line .value { color: #1d4ed8; }\nbody.colour-blue .seal-ring { stroke: #1d4ed8; }\nbody.colour-blue .seal-star { fill: #1d4ed8; }\nbody.colour-blue .frame,\nbody.colour-blue .frame-inner { border-color: #1d4ed8; }\nbody.colour-blue .recipient { border-bottom-color: #dbeafe; }\n\nbody.colour-gold .eyebrow,\nbody.colour-gold .recipient,\nbody.colour-gold .score-line .value { color: #a16207; }\nbody.colour-gold .seal-ring { stroke: #a16207; }\nbody.colour-gold .seal-star { fill: #a16207; }\nbody.colour-gold .frame,\nbody.colour-gold .frame-inner { border-color: #a16207; }\nbody.colour-gold .recipient { border-bottom-color: #fef3c7; }\n</style>\n\n<body class=\"family-{{ doc.layout_family }} colour-{{ doc.layout_colour }}\">\n<div class=\"certificate\">\n\t<div class=\"frame\"></div>\n\t<div class=\"frame-inner\"></div>\n\n\t{% if doc.is_test %}\n\t<div class=\"watermark\">{{ _(\"Sample\") }}</div>\n\t{% elif not doc.passed %}\n\t<div class=\"not-passed-flag\">{{ _(\"Not Passed\") }}</div>\n\t{% endif %}\n\n\t<div class=\"main\">\n\t\t<p class=\"eyebrow\">{{ _(\"Certificate\") }}</p>\n\t\t<h1 class=\"title\">{{ _(\"Certificate of Achievement\") }}</h1>\n\t\t<p class=\"lead\">{{ _(\"This certifies that\") }}</p>\n\t\t<div class=\"recipient\">{{ doc.recipient_name | e }}</div>\n\t\t<p class=\"lead\">{{ _(\"has successfully completed\") }}</p>\n\t\t<div class=\"survey-title\">{{ doc.survey_title | e }}</div>\n\t\t<p class=\"score-line\">\n\t\t\t{{ _(\"Scored\") }} <span class=\"value\">{{ \"%.1f\"|format(doc.score_percentage) }}%</span>\n\t\t\t{{ _(\"against a required\") }} <span class=\"value\">{{ \"%.0f\"|format(doc.passing_score) }}%</span>\n\t\t</p>\n\t\t{% if doc.section_breakdown %}\n\t\t{% set ns = namespace(correct=0, partial=0, incorrect=0) %}\n\t\t{% for row in doc.section_breakdown %}\n\t\t\t{% set ns.correct = ns.correct + row.correct %}\n\t\t\t{% set ns.partial = ns.partial + row.partial %}\n\t\t\t{% set ns.incorrect = ns.incorrect + row.incorrect %}\n\t\t{% endfor %}\n\t\t<p class=\"summary-line\">\n\t\t\t{{ ns.correct }} {{ _(\"correct\") }} &middot;\n\t\t\t{{ ns.partial }} {{ _(\"partial\") }} &middot;\n\t\t\t{{ ns.incorrect }} {{ _(\"incorrect\") }}\n\t\t</p>\n\t\t{% endif %}\n\t</div>\n\n\t<div class=\"footer\">\n\t\t<div class=\"cell block\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"value\">{{ doc.issue_date }}</div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"line\">{{ _(\"Date Issued\") }}</div>\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div class=\"cell seal-cell\">\n\t\t\t<svg class=\"seal\" viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\">\n\t\t\t\t<circle class=\"seal-ring\" cx=\"50\" cy=\"50\" r=\"46\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n\t\t\t\t<circle class=\"seal-ring\" cx=\"50\" cy=\"50\" r=\"36\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n\t\t\t\t<path class=\"seal-star\" d=\"M50 26 L56 42 L73 42 L59 52 L64 68 L50 58 L36 68 L41 52 L27 42 L44 42 Z\"/>\n\t\t\t</svg>\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div class=\"cell block\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"value\">{{ doc.certificate_number }}</div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"line\">{{ _(\"Certificate No.\") }}</div>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</div>\n</div>\n</body>\n",
